; Reason: better-auth declares a peerOptional on vitest@^4, but the test suite is pinned
; to vitest@3.2.4 by @vitest/coverage-v8. npm treats even an optional peer as a hard
; ERESOLVE failure here, so a plain `npm install` aborts on the root project.
;
; This was previously worked around by typing --legacy-peer-deps on every install, which
; deploy/deploy.sh does not do - so the script died on its first step and the deploy had
; to be hand-rolled. Setting it here makes the flag apply everywhere, including CI.
;
; Only the root project needs this; apps/admin, api-server and websocket-server all
; resolve cleanly without it. Revisit when better-auth supports vitest 3.x as a peer.
legacy-peer-deps=true
